  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reading for East Africas Development (READ)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Learners in East Africa will have improved access to a high-quality basic education under the United States Agency for International Development (USAID) Reading for East Africas Development (READ) project. The project is meant to improve student learning outcomes and expand access to basic education, particularly for marginalized and vulnerable learners in Ethiopia, Kenya, Rwanda, Tanzania, and Uganda. Activities for the READ project are mainly focused on, but not limited to, improving reading skills. Illustrative examples of tasks could include supporting governments in improving teacher effectiveness, strengthening student assessments, addressing the needs of learners with disabilities and other marginalized learners, and other activities.</narrative>
  </description>
